{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Betzalel son of Uri, etc., made all that YHWH commanded Moses.</b> It is not written here 'all that Moses commanded,' but 'all that YHWH commanded Moses' — even things that his teacher did not tell him, his mind agreed with what was said to Moses at Sinai. For Moses commanded Betzalel to make first the vessels and afterward the Mishkan. Betzalel said to him: the way of the world is to first make a house and afterward put vessels inside it. He said to him: Thus I heard from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He. Moses said to him: you were indeed בְּצֵל אֵל, 'in the shadow of El' — for certainly thus did the Holy One, blessed be He, command me. And so he did: the Mishkan first, and afterward he made the vessels."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:50.198870447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}